==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Cleanerbot Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Green Shell Cat''' when obtained from [[March to Death (Merciless)|March to Death]] (guaranteed to drop) and is level 20 or above.

==Strategy/Usage==
The god of early-stage stalling, Curling Cat is notable for its extremely long backswing, low cost, very high health, lots of immunities and singular knockback. It can be used instead of meatshields to wall peons for a very long time in stages where few enemies spawn at the start or only spawn the main threats on base hit. It can also be used to great effect against long-ranged enemies when supported by [[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Long Distance]] cats, being able to stall the foes in [[Heavenly Tower/Floor 39|Heavenly Tower Floor 39]] almost entirely on its own, or it can hold a heavy pusher in place for an attacker to land a hit. For example, it allows [[Crazed Moneko (Special Cat)|Crazed Moneko]] or [[Cheerleader Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Soba Cat]] to land a hit on [[Super Metal Hippoe]] or [[Sir Metal Seal]], which is usually not possible without assistance due to these enemies' extreme pushing power and the critical hitters' slow attack animations.

==='''True Form'''===
Green Shell Cat is a straight improvement over its other forms. Thanks to its extra movement speed and health, it can be relied upon much more; it has a much better chance of stalling a group of enemies early in a stage, making it possible to summon another when one dies in many instances where it was not possible. Despite the difficulty of [[March to Death (Merciless)|the stage it is obtained from]], it is recommended to unlock this form as soon as possible if you cannot get its previous form to work in a stage where you need him, such as some appearances of [[Professor A.]] in {{4c}} [[Stories of Legend]].

