==Trivia==
*Cleanerbot Cat has the third lowest attack frequency in the game, being beaten out by [[Stealth Cat (Special Cat)|Surprise Stealth Cat]] and then [[Ancient Egg: N112 (Rare Cat)|Cat Egg Pod]].
*Curling Cat was among the units granted [[Immune to Warp]] in [[Version 6.5 Update|Version 6.5]].
*Green Shell Cat is a reference to the shell of a [[mariowiki:Koopa Troopa|Green Koopa Troopa]] from the [[mariowiki:Mario (series)|Mario]] franchise.
*Curling Cat is one of the units to have its descriptions rewritten in [[Version 14.5 Update|Version 14.5]], as "Unharmed by wave attacks" was changed to "Immune to Waves".
*Cleanerbot Cat used to be named Zamboney Cat prior to [[Version 15.0 Update|Version 15.0]].
**Zamboney Cat's name came from zamboni, a common alias for an [[wikipedia:Ice resurfacer|ice resurfacing machine]].
***Despite the old name, it bears a much greater resemblance to a [[wikipedia:Robotic vacuum cleaner|Robotic vacuum cleaner]], which is supported by the Japanese description referring to it as a cleaning robot, and likely the reason for the name change.
**Cleanerbot Cat's name change was not carried over to the Nintendo Switch port, it is still called Zamboney Cat.

